{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "A Quick Coffee Break"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Restaurant Tales"}, {"type": "position", "content": 5}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 10}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Accurately use important information about people's jobs and places of work in communicative situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn6le10ob05re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "tale"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a story about imaginary events"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The cook remembered some of her restaurant tales."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le10ob05aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you tell stories about work."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to realize"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to understand or become aware of something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They were able to realize he used the wrong vegetables."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le10ob05aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to substitute"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to use something in place of something else"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He realized it was a mistake to substitute the vegetables."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le10ob05aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "awful"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "really bad"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She felt the cook's mistake was awful."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le10ob05aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to make a mess"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to cause something to get dirty."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She was glad not to make a mess of things in her job."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le10ob05aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to admit"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to realize or accept the truth about something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The cook was able to admit his mistakes to the boss."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le10ob05aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to deduct"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to take away something from the total"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She never had any penalty deducted from her paycheck."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le10ob05aud07"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Showing Interest, Enthusiasm, and Sympathy"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use certain expressions to show interest at what someone is talking about.<br>There are expressions to show that you are enthusiastic about an idea.<br>There are also expressions to show sympathy at some sad news or someone's feelings."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The following table contain examples of expressions that show interest, enthusiasm, or surprise."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Interest</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Please do tell.<br> Then what happened? <br>Hey, what's going on?</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Enthusiasm</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Wow! That's great.<br> Awesome. Let's do it.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Sympathy</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Oh, that's too bad. <br>Oh, that's unfortunate.<br> Oh, that must be difficult. <br>I'm sorry to hear that.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "What I didn't or haven't done!"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When talking about actions that you have never done you need or you never did when you had the opportunity, you need to use <span class=\"strong\">SIMPLE PAST</span> and <span class=\"strong\">PRESENT PERFECT</span> in <span class=\"italic\">negative</span>. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Remember you use <span class=\"strong\">SIMPLE PAST</span> to talk about finished actions in a specific time. And you use <span class=\"strong\">PRESENT PERFECT</span> to talk about actions that started in the past and haven't finished or are still related to the present. "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":1,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">SIMPLE PAST</span> in negative:    Subject + auxiliary + NOT + <span class=\\\"italic\\\">verb in base form</span> + complement <br><br>  <span class=\\\"strong\\\">\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"  I/you/they/we/he/she + <span class=\\\"strong\\\">did</span> + not  (didn't) + <span class=\\\"italic\\\">infinitive</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"  I/you/they/we + <span class=\\\"strong\\\">were</span> + not  (weren't)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"  He/she/it + <span class=\\\"strong\\\">was</span> + not  (wasn't)\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": " The customers <span class=\"strong\">didn</span><span class=\"italic\">'t notice</span> the difference."}, {"type": "example", "content": "They <span class=\"strong\">didn</span><span class=\"italic\">'t deduct</span> my payment. "}, {"type": "example", "content": " The taste <span class=\"strong\">was</span><span class=\"italic\">n't</span> bad. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "They <span class=\"strong\">were</span></span><span class=\"italic\">n't</span> here 2 weeks ago. "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":1,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"strong\\\">PRESENT PERFECT</span> in negative Form: Subject + auxiliary + NOT + <span class=\\\"italic\\\">verb in past participle</span> + complement \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"  I/you/we/they + <span class=\\\"strong\\\">have</span> + NOT (haven't) + <span class=\\\"italic\\\">verb in past participle</span> + complement \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"She/he/it + <span class=\\\"strong\\\">has</span> + NOT (hasn't) + <span class=\\\"italic\\\">verb in past participle</span> + complement \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": " I <span class=\"strong\">have</span><span class=\"italic\">n't made</span> a mess like that in my new job."}, {"type": "example", "content": "The new cook <span class=\"strong\">has</span><span class=\"italic\">n't admitted</span> his mistake."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Think about a major mistake you have made at work or at school."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write at least 8 sentences about what happened. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use present perfect tense and simple past tense."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read your story to your partner. Ask your partner to tell you in English about a similar experience."}]}, {"type": "take